The attached image (Fig. 9 from Journal of Controlled Release and Fig. 1 from npj Vaccines) demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the antibody response to adsorbed antigens. Mice injected with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) formulated with Nano-11 or aluminum hydroxide (AH) showed substantially higher anti-rPA IgG titers compared to rPA alone. Nano-11, across tested doses, induced antibody levels comparable to or even superior to AH, particularly at lower concentrations (e.g., 12.5 µg/dose Nano-11 vs. AH), highlighting its potent immunopotentiating effect. These results support Nano-11's efficacy as a vaccine adjuvant.